<ContentLayout
  title="Workshop & Crafting"
  description="ARC Raiders crafting guide: blueprints, materials, gunsmith upgrades and what to build first in your Speranza workshop."
  eyebrow="Workshop & Crafting"
  heading="What to build, and in what order"
  lede="Your workshop is the reason to extract. Materials you carry out convert into better gear, which lets you take bigger risks on the next run — but only if you spend them in the right order."
>
  <h2>How crafting is gated</h2>
  <p>
    Weapons fall into two categories. A small number — the Ferro and Stitcher
    among them — are craftable from the start with no blueprint requirement. The
    majority are blueprint-locked: crafting does not unlock at all until you find
    the blueprint. Blueprints drop during raids, and some blueprint-locked
    weapons can be bought outright from a dealer instead, which is often faster
    than waiting on the drop.
  </p>
  <p>
    Separately, your Gunsmith level gates which weapon ranks you can produce.
    Rank IV variants are a meaningful step up rather than a marginal one, so
    Gunsmith progression is worth prioritising over breadth.
  </p>

  <h2>Materials worth stopping for</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Used for</th><th>Priority</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Metal parts</strong></td><td>Core weapon crafting — a Ferro costs five.</td><td>Always pick up</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Rubber</strong></td><td>Weapon crafting alongside metal.</td><td>Always pick up</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Steel springs</strong></td><td>Weapon attachments.</td><td>High</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>ARC parts</strong></td><td>Upgrades. Comes off destroyed machines.</td><td>High</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>ARC Alloy</strong></td><td>Higher-tier crafting. Drops from heavy ARC and bosses.</td><td>High, situational</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Advanced ARC Powercell</strong></td><td>Endgame crafting. Boss drop.</td><td>Take every one you see</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Author note:</strong> exact recipe costs beyond the well-documented
      ones above shift with balance patches. Verify current numbers against the
      in-game crafting screen before publishing a full recipe table — outdated
      material costs are the fastest way to lose reader trust.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build order for a new Raider</h2>
  <ol class="ordered">
    <li><strong>Ferro, repeatedly.</strong> No blueprint, cheap, punches far above its rarity. Craft several and accept that you will lose some.</li>
    <li><strong>Gunsmith upgrades.</strong> Access to higher weapon ranks changes more than any single new gun will.</li>
    <li><strong>Stash and storage capacity.</strong> Running out of room is a real constraint, and expeditions add permanent stash space on top.</li>
    <li><strong>Anvil access.</strong> Either find the blueprint or buy it from a dealer. It becomes your default secondary for a long time.</li>
    <li><strong>Attachment production.</strong> Muzzle brakes, grips and silencers change weapon feel substantially — a Silencer III on a Tempest makes it one of the quietest options in the game.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Currencies</h2>
  <p>
    Coins are the general-purpose currency and the main reason to farm high-value
    maps like Buried City and Stella Montis. The Cred system has been retired —
    Embark confirmed leftover Cred expired with the October 8, 2026 Frozen Trail
    update, replaced by a new reward system. Rewards already claimed were kept.
    Check the <a href="/seasons">Seasons &amp; Updates</a> page for the current
    state of this, since it changed recently.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>

